   "resumo_en": "On the Boards is the second album by Irish rock band Taste. It was recorded in London in September/October 1969 and released on 9 January 1970. It is their final studio album and the release that brought Rory Gallagher to prominence, reaching number 18 on the UK Albums Chart. Reviewers have praised its variety and the precision of its ensemble playing, and noted the jazz inflections of Gallagher's guitar and his unaffected vocals. Lester Bangs dubbed it \"impressive ... progressive blues\".",
